    "# The Retriever's Role in a RAG System\n",
    "\n",
    "## How your retriever fits into a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture\n",
    "A Retriever return the most relevant document's to a query\n",
    "## How it works with a generator model (e.g., a large language model)\n",
    "The retrieved document's are used to build the context to the query\n",
    "## How this architecture powers real-world tools like ChatGPT, Copilot, or Perplexity\n",
    "The answer to the query in real world tools is then obtained from the generated context\n",
    "## What your comparison reveals about the evolution from keyword search (BM25) to static embeddings (Word2Vec) to transformer-based semantic search\n",
    "Retrival quality improves but compute costs, memory cost, memory use and latency also increase.\n",
